  <section class="section-gap seo-concept-definition">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="seo-concept-answer-card reveal">
        <h2>What is Generative Engine Optimization?</h2>
        <p class="seo-concept-answer-lead"><strong>Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) is the practice of structuring a website and its supporting content so that generative AI systems &mdash; ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Gemini, and Copilot &mdash; retrieve it, trust it, and cite it when answering user questions.</strong></p>
        <p>Traditional SEO competes for a position in a ranked list. GEO competes to be one of the handful of sources a language model actually pulls into its answer. The two overlap, but they are not the same job: an AI system weighs entity clarity, factual consistency across the open web, extractable structure, and third-party corroboration far more heavily than it weighs keyword placement.</p>
        <dl class="seo-concept-definition-grid">
          <div>
            <dt>SEO</dt>
            <dd>Earns a ranked position on a results page. Success is measured in rankings, clicks, and organic sessions.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>AIO</dt>
            <dd>Makes your own pages machine-readable, so AI systems can parse what you do. Success is measured in extraction accuracy.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>GEO</dt>
            <dd>Earns a citation inside the generated answer itself. Success is measured in share of voice across AI answers and referral traffic from AI surfaces.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

