      <div class="seo-concept-faq-list reveal">
        <details class="seo-concept-faq-item" open>
          <summary>How is GEO different from standard SEO?</summary>
          <p>SEO competes for a ranked position on a results page. GEO competes to be one of the sources a generative engine quotes inside its answer. Ranking well helps, but it is not sufficient &mdash; AI systems weigh entity clarity, factual consistency across the wider web, extractable page structure, and third-party corroboration far more heavily than keyword placement.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-concept-faq-item">
          <summary>How is GEO different from AIO?</summary>
          <p>AIO (AI Optimization) makes your own pages machine-readable so AI systems can understand what you do. GEO uses that foundation to earn citations inside generated answers, which also depends on sources you do not own. Most brands need both; AIO is usually the prerequisite.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-concept-faq-item">
          <summary>Which AI engines do you optimize for?</summary>
          <p>ChatGPT Search, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Google Gemini, and Microsoft Copilot. We track each separately because they retrieve from different source mixes and cite very differently for the same question.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-concept-faq-item">
          <summary>Can generative engine visibility actually be measured?</summary>
          <p>Yes, though not the way rankings are. We define a fixed set of commercial prompts, run them on a schedule against each engine, and record whether your brand is cited, how it is described, and which competitors appear alongside you. Alongside that we segment referral sessions arriving from AI surfaces in GA4.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-concept-faq-item">
          <summary>How long does GEO take to show results?</summary>
          <p>Structural fixes &mdash; schema, entity consistency, crawler access, answer-first page rebuilds &mdash; are typically in place within 4 to 8 weeks, and engines that recrawl frequently can reflect them quickly. Citation share driven by third-party corroboration moves more slowly and usually compounds over 3 to 6 months.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="seo-concept-faq-item">
          <summary>Do I still need traditional SEO if I invest in GEO?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Generative engines draw heavily on the conventional search index, so organic authority remains an input to AI visibility. GEO extends SEO into answer surfaces; it does not replace it.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
